# ================================================================
# CENZONTLE Web — Environment Variables
# ================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values. Do NOT commit it.
# Full variable reference: docs/configuration.md
# ================================================================

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Server-only URL for the BFF proxy (never exposed to the client bundle).
# The Playwright config also derives the port it binds the API to from this
# value. The proxy forwards the caller's real Auth0 access token, so there is
# no shared secret between web and api.
API_INTERNAL_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Absolute path of the monorepo on the API host — the working directory the
# embedded Claude Code terminal starts in (TerminalService resolves the git
# repo from it with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`). It does NOT gate the
# "Abrir Claude Code" ("Open Claude Code") button: that button always renders
# and always opens the terminal page. What refuses is the destination — with
# this variable empty the terminal skips its auto-start and prints a message
# telling you to configure it. There is no compiled-in fallback, deliberately:
# an absolute host path would leak into the browser bundle.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PROJECT_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/your/CENZONTLE/clone

# ================================================================
# Auth0 Configuration (SDK v4)
# ================================================================
# 1. Create a "Regular Web Application" in Auth0 Dashboard > Applications
#    - Name: Cenzontle Web
#
# 2. Configure in Auth0 Application Settings:
#    - Allowed Callback URLs: http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
#    - Allowed Logout URLs:   http://localhost:3000
#    - Allowed Web Origins:   http://localhost:3000
#
# 3. Copy values below from Auth0 Application Settings:

# Auth0 domain (without https://)
AUTH0_DOMAIN=YOUR_TENANT.auth0.com

# Application Client ID and Secret
AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=
AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Random secret (min 32 chars): openssl rand -hex 32
AUTH0_SECRET=

# App base URL
APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# API audience (must match API Identifier in Auth0 > APIs)
AUTH0_AUDIENCE=https://api.cenzontle.app

# OPTIONAL — machine-to-machine app. It powers step-up authentication
# (re-confirming your password before epic sign-offs, both Forge gates and DEV
# branch alignment) and every "Equipo" ("Team") screen through the Auth0
# Management API. Same values as in apps/api/.env.
#
# Leave them empty and the behavior splits on NODE_ENV, exactly as on the API
# side (apps/api/src/modules/auth/auth.service.ts:88-116):
#   - NODE_ENV=production → /auth/verify-password returns 503 and every
#     sign-off and gate is blocked.
#   - anything else, INCLUDING NODE_ENV unset → the API logs a [DEV BYPASS]
#     warning and approves WITHOUT checking the password at all. Fine for local
#     development, a hole anywhere else: a staging or demo instance that does
#     not set NODE_ENV=production inherits the bypass, so anyone holding a
#     valid session can sign off. Set NODE_ENV=production on every deployed
#     environment, or configure the M2M app.
# Details: docs/auth0-setup.md, docs/configuration.md.
#
# The Equipo screens have no such fallback: without these two the
# client_credentials token request fails
# (apps/web/src/lib/auth0-management.ts:15-26) and every team operation errors
# out — the member list just renders empty.
# AUTH0_M2M_CLIENT_ID=
# AUTH0_M2M_CLIENT_SECRET=
